{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Payload-shape archaeology (2026-09-06): ADR 0107 is the canonical decision record. It decides `OutboundUpdatePayload` for (outbound, update): at least one of `changed_fields` / `comments` / `labels` / `links` must be non-empty, and `as_legacy_dict()` emits the wrapped shape `{changed_fields, comments, labels, links, local_id}`. This ticket’s description and earthborn-statuelike-boutu point back to that ADR.\n\nCurrent-code evidence favors the wrapped/typed shape for outbound. `outbound_pass.py` constructs `OutboundUpdatePayload(...)` directly; `mutation_payloads.py` validates and serializes the wrapped contract; `single-vast-roan` records the cutover/live DC evidence: outbound_pass constructs typed create/update/delete payloads, `_mutation_to_batch_dict` reads `.fields` / `.changed_fields` unambiguously, and typed-only DC convergence passed. Legacy `differ.py` still has an older flat `payload=changed` outbound/update emitter, so that is the migration surface, not the precedent.\n\nVerdict: resolved-with-evidence. Recommendation for this outbound ticket: migrate the older differ.py outbound/update path to wrapped `changed_fields` / typed `OutboundUpdatePayload`, because ADR 0107 and the newest cutover code already chose that shape."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788763468333352001,"uuid":"0f712d10-621c-4d32-912d-415b33671353"}